.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Anchored to the repo root with a leading slash. Unanchored, `memory/` also
# matches a nested one — e.g. a `templates/test-fixtures/memory/` — so any new
# file added there is silently unaddable and shows nothing in `git status`.
# That bit agent-ready-projects, which anchored its own in v1.19.0. No nested
# `memory/` exists here today, so this changes nothing now; it is preventive.
# `audits/` and `docs/work-items/` are anchored for the same reason.
/memory/
/audits/
/docs/work-items/

# Papers are confidential-by-default; allowlist public framework demos explicitly.
# A new papers/<name>/ is invisible to git until you add a matching `!papers/<name>` line.
#
# DECIDED 2026-08-16, and the reason matters more than the rule: **this repo is
# public because it is a general tool.** That makes the allowlist a publishing
# decision, not a tracking convenience.
#
# So: **never add a `!papers/<name>` line for a paper that audits, reviews or
# critiques work this project did not author.** Such a directory stays ignored
# permanently — not pending a later review, not once the author has been told.
# Version-controlling a critique of a named third party would publish it as a
# side effect, and that is not a trade this project makes. At least one such
# audit exists on the maintainer's disk and is deliberately not named here:
# naming the instance in a tracked file leaks exactly what ignoring it protects.
# The same reasoning already anchors `/audits/` above.
#
# `!papers/perspective` is allowlisted because it is this project's OWN paper,
# written to be published — the one category where the publishing decision is
# already settled.
papers/*
!papers/perspective

# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz

# Python (tools/, tests/)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
